 "description": "The Saffier SC 6.50 Cruise is a true classic daysailer, combining timeless lines with modern engineering and advanced hardware. Her elegant design has stood the test of time, while recent updates bring her fully up to date. Compact yet seaworthy, she comfortably seats up to six people and sails with precision and ease.",
 "credits": [
  {
   "label": "Design",
   "value": "R. Hennevanger"
  }
 ],
 "awards": [],
 "sections": [
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Classic lines, modern technology",
   "intro": "With her timeless look and updated design, the SC 6.50 Cruise blends tradition and innovation. The new rig features a large mainsail and a self-tacking jib, offering excellent upwind capabilities.\nShe can easily be fitted with a furling code zero for more power downwind. Combined with a bulb keel that lowers the centre of gravity, a deep spade rudder, and an optimized sail plan, this compact daysailer delivers surprising performance and precise control in various conditions.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Sailing solo, or together",
   "intro": "The Sc 6.50 Cruise is built for freedom on the water - whether sailing solo or together. The cockpit is very comfortable, with smart details like integrated cup holders and hidden storage for halyards and control lines.\nAll lines run back to the helm, so you can easily sail her solo while staying fully in control. The layout feels open and practical, offering enough space to move around with ease. For longer trips, there's even a small cabin with enough space to stay overnight.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Very seaworthy",
   "intro": "The Saffier SC 6.50 Cruise is built with confidence at sea in mind. A 50% ballast ratio gives strong stability and a controlled feel in changing conditions, adding safety and trust when the wind picks up.\nA modern rig design, combined with a bulb keel and a deep spade rudder, creates balance and direct control. The result is a steady, predictable daysailer that responds well to every helm input.\n\nShe feels at home both in lakes and coastal waters.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Esthec decking",
   "intro": "Esthec offers the timeless look of natural teak with none of the maintenance. Durable and wear-resistant, it keeps your deck looking sharp without any extra effort.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Effortless single-handed sailing",
   "intro": "Designed with simplicity in mind, the SC 6.50 Cruise is easy to sail alone. With a self-tacking jib and furling Code Zero, you're in full control from the helm.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Spacious cockpit",
   "intro": "With space for up to six people, the cockpit is perfect for sharing the experience with friends or family—or simply enjoying the view on your own while sailing in peace.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  },
  {
   "kind": "block",
   "id": null,
   "title": "Diesel or electric propulsion",
   "intro": "Choose the propulsion that fits your style—quiet electric power or classic diesel. Both integrate seamlessly and match the spirit of easy cruising.",
   "items": [],
   "images": []
  }
 ],
